From 762bc880130c4ada14bc0b4832066a72f5988500 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yang Tsao <yang@fydeos.io>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:43:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 47/75] display: reflect external displays as ON, don't
 power-manage them (ARC)

On fydroid the external HDMI panel is owned and powered by Chrome OS,
which surfaces it to SurfaceFlinger (via the wayland-backed composer)
only while it is connected and on. Android must reflect that state, not
drive it. Previously the external display's DisplayPowerController was
never handed a power request (mPowerRequest=null), so its state stayed
STATE_UNKNOWN; DisplayManagerService then set the viewport isActive=false
and apps (e.g. a customer-facing Presentation on the second screen) could
not target the display.

For external displays only, mark the device FLAG_NEVER_BLANK so DMS skips
both the DPC power request and the state push against the Chrome-owned
panel, and report STATE_ON so getDisplays()/Presentation see a usable
display. The internal panel is untouched and keeps normal power
management.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: If632deec2b9a68ef97f7db4e71863f1e4ae97ec7
---
 .../server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java       | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
index 58a182a61e44..59a37a8ed7a6 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/LocalDisplayAdapter.java
@@ -704,6 +704,21 @@ final class LocalDisplayAdapter extends DisplayAdapter {
                     mInfo.flags |= DisplayDeviceInfo.FLAG_PRESENTATION;
                     mInfo.name = getContext().getResources().getString(
                             com.android.internal.R.string.display_manager_hdmi_display_name);
+                    // FydeOS/fydroid: external displays are owned and powered by Chrome
+                    // OS, which surfaces them to SurfaceFlinger (via the wayland-backed
+                    // composer) only while they are connected and turned on. Android must
+                    // reflect that state, never drive it: without this, the display's
+                    // DisplayPowerController is never handed a power request, so its state
+                    // stays STATE_UNKNOWN, its viewport reports isActive=false, and apps
+                    // (e.g. a Presentation on the second screen) cannot target it.
+                    //
+                    // Mark the display never-blank so PowerManager/DMS skip running power
+                    // management (setPowerMode) against the Chrome-owned panel, and report
+                    // it as ON so getDisplays()/Presentation see a usable display. Chrome
+                    // hot-unplugs the display when it powers off, so "surfaced" == "on".
+                    mInfo.flags |= DisplayDeviceInfo.FLAG_NEVER_BLANK;
+                    mInfo.state = Display.STATE_ON;
+                    mInfo.committedState = Display.STATE_ON;
                 }
                 mInfo.frameRateOverrides = mFrameRateOverrides;
 
